{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014","id":34206,"title":"Wraith 20th; Late 2014","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-20T18:17:49-08:00","id":34206,"title":"Wraith 20th; Late 2014","content":"So Wraith 20th is due late 2014, supposedly for the fall. <br /> <br /> So what do you want in a Wr20 book? What do you think has happened to the Underworld since the End of Days, the Last Great Maelstorm* and other assorted troubles? <br /> <br /> *Not to be confused for the Last Great Time War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T18:43:18-08:00","id":34219,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I\u2019m curious to see what direction the Stygian metaplot goes. Will the events from <i>Ends of Empire</i> be ignored? Perhaps altered slightly so that Charon has returned as the Stygian Emperor? Or, will they go with the establishment of the \u201cNew\u201d Deathlords from EOE, each one reigning over a new Legion?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to see a solid narrative-foundation for the necrography [sic] of the Underworld. Where the dead can go, how they get there, etc. Maybe even a get an \u201cofficial\u201d answer to my Space Ghost question (however ridiculous the premise was). <br /> <br /> Chains and corpus and howling tempest winds and shrouds and spectres; I can\u2019t wait to see what ectoplasmic wonders the Underworld has wrought in last umpteen years\u2026<br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T19:06:06-08:00","id":34228,"title":"","content":"These 20th Anniversary Editions aren't full new editions/revisions of the game lines, or rules, but rather a nod and modest updating of the game to a contemporary timeline and to combine all of what makes the game and it's core setting into one tome (or as much as possible.)<br /> <br /> I they follow in the footsteps of V20 and W20, you're likely not going to see a continuation events after End of Days... in fact, the Time of Judgement and much of that metaplot has been wiped clean or leaving only a shadow on the mechanics within the game, and hasn't shown in the &quot;story&quot; either. So... the rule book will contain the mechanics of everything, but as far as &quot;setting&quot; goes, expect that those &quot;OMG, the end is here!&quot; stuff just won't have happened and instead the end of the world was stretched out to beyond tomorrow.<br /> <br /> V20's SAS was &quot;Dust to Dust&quot;, an indirect child of the original storyline of Chicago that ran through the V:tM books and pre-gen games. The rule book contains not only the lost Clans, but different versions of Clans (the different Malks), and (almost) all of the Bloodlines too.<br /> W20's SAS referenced the death of Sam Haight, but continued that story of &quot;The Skinner&quot;. The rule books contain revisions to history, backed up and moved forward (the evil werelion Black Tooth is still alive, but the all-inclusive African Fera movement (the Ahadi) are around and active. <br /> <br /> This is all different from what the Mage the Ascension (Revised): Convention Books (everything but &quot;Iteration X Revised&quot;) recently did, which was to finish up a line of books that were set exactly within the Revised edition, but rather than all taking place in 2004, they were updated to 2012-2013... and talked a bit about what happened after the ToJ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T19:30:50-08:00","id":34237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014#post34206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Not to be confused for the Last Great Time War.</div> </div> </div> </div>All such conflicts may be related to the Last Great Time War. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Errr, anyway, I'd like support for Risen characters in the rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T19:50:17-08:00","id":34245,"title":"","content":"A couple of notes:<br /> <br /> - Wraith20 was <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">announced in August</a> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fq76822ciWI#t=44m8s\" target=\"_blank\">at GenCon</a> and has been <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule\" target=\"_blank\">on our schedule since</a>.<br /> - Wraith will be our first X20 for a game which did not have a Revised edition. We're discussing whether or not to take the opportunity to update it to Revised edition standards, or if being a nostalgia product should take precedence. So it's <i>possible</i> that it may end up being a proper new edition. We'll see.<br /> - &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maelstrom\" target=\"_blank\">Maelstrom</a>,&quot; not &quot;maelstorm.&quot; Common misteak.<br /> - Undoubtedly we'll continue our metaplot-agnostic approach from previous X20 rulebooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T20:00:05-08:00","id":34247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=34245#post34245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maelstrom\" target=\"_blank\">Maelstrom</a>,&quot; not &quot;maelstorm.&quot; Common misteak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I giggled.<br /> <br /> I would like to see Wraith updated to Revised mechanics, but the most significant is just the addition of Bashing damage which.. doesn't affect Wraiths that much since to them, B/L are basically the same.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T20:00:26-08:00","id":34248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=34245#post34245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Common misteak.</div> </div> </div> </div> And in keeping with the theme...<br /> <img src=\"http://i3.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/268/555/60f.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Also, please, <i>please</i> update the rule set to Revised/20th.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T22:11:33-08:00","id":34296,"title":"","content":"The issues with Wraith, in terms of the Time of Judgement, is that &quot;Ends of Empire&quot; happened several years before the actual ToJ. So maybe Wr2o will be pre-EoE, and maybe not. Originally, the Dark Empire of Iron had dissolved almost five years before things went ass up for everyone else. There is no way to resolve this issue which will not create other issues. <br /> <br /> And a specter is responsible for misspelling &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maelstrom\" target=\"_blank\">Maelstrom</a>&quot; and that is my story and I am sticking to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T04:16:10-08:00","id":34389,"title":"","content":"I think we're jumping the gun a bit. Mage 20 hasn't even debuted yet and we all know that in order to update and yet set back Wraith, a lot of changes might have to be made. I think it's pretty pre-mature to start guessing/asking/demanding what Wr20 will be all about. I for one am really happy that they've set a date for a possible Wraith 20 at all. Let's start with the small objectives first. Maybe we'll finally get all these Wraith topics their own forum finally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T07:08:49-08:00","id":34432,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=34389#post34389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's pretty pre-mature to start guessing/asking/demanding what Wr20 will be all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such speculations are the natural by-products of the elusive phenomenon known as \u201chope.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=34389#post34389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe we'll finally get all these Wraith topics their own forum finally?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watch out! It looks like you\u2019re catching it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, I know I\u2019m jumping the Maggot Revolver a bit, but it\u2019s fun to consider.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=34296#post34296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issues with Wraith, in terms of the Time of Judgement, is that &quot;Ends of Empire&quot; happened several years before the actual ToJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I\u2019m curious to see what route they with go with. In the other TOJ books, players were presented with multiple scenarios on how to bring about their particular Splatapocalypses; Wraith had one \u201cofficial\u201d-ish ending.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T08:09:00-08:00","id":34455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=34228#post34228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is all different from what the Mage the Ascension (Revised): Convention Books (everything but &quot;Iteration X Revised&quot;) recently did, which was to finish up a line of books that were set exactly within the Revised edition, but rather than all taking place in 2004, they were updated to 2012-2013... and talked a bit about what happened after the ToJ.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the universe of the recent CBs has the early events leading up the ToJ has happened, chief among the Avatar Storm and the appearance of the Red Star but that's all that happened and time moved on. The events of the ToJ could still happen but they haven't.<br /> <br /> Anyway Wr20 will be pre-6GM otherwise they'd have to rebuild much, if not all of the setting which they won't do for the Wr20 Rulebook for the exact reasons others have mentioned. Though I would be nice to have a later book all about a post-6GM Underworld.<br /> <br /> What I want to see in the Wr20 Rulebook:<br /> -a full list of Stygian Arcanoi, including variations found in other books<br /> -at least a basic overview of the geography of the Underworld<br /> -at least a basic overview of all the other Dark Kingdoms, from the Dark Kingdom of Jade to the Dark Kingdom of Wire, though I can understand not giving us their unique Arcanoi in this book<br /> -a mention of Orpheus and potential connections with Wr20<br /> <br /> What supplements I would like to see for Wr20:<br /> -new Guild Books, whether its one big book covering the Guilds, a couple books covering several Guilds or a whole new line of GBs<br /> -a book on the geography of the Underworld, not just on the make-up of the Underworld but on some of the more prominent Necropolis and places<br /> -a book bridging Orpheus with Wraith<br /> -a book dealing with how the Underworld could be like post-6GM<br /> -a book discussing the other Dark Kingdoms, what they're like, what Arcanoi they possess, etc.<br /> <br /> EDIT:I forgot but another thing I want to see in the Wr20 Rulebook is a writeup on the Risen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","user":"AkatsukiLeader13","date":". 12-22-2013, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T09:53:47-08:00","id":34977,"title":"","content":"Never mind me, just sitting here in the corner, taking notes...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T10:25:38-08:00","id":35003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=34455#post34455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually the universe of the recent CBs has the early events leading up the ToJ has happened, chief among the Avatar Storm and the appearance of the Red Star but that's all that happened and time moved on. The events of the ToJ could still happen but they haven't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that the Convention Books were the last releases of the Revised era and are not Mage20 books. While the CBs take place in a post-Storm world which never saw the events of Ascenion, Mage20 works under the default assumption that there is no Avatar Storm (yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T11:54:47-08:00","id":35041,"title":"","content":"I'm well aware of that, I was just addressing Torakhan's previous post about the setting of the CBs. I never said they were part of M20's default setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T11:46:36-08:00","id":40615,"title":"","content":"I definitely want to see the Wr20 book cover all of the currently printed Arcanoi. All of the setting discussion, etc that we would expect. I want at least 4 pages on each of the Dark Kingdoms. So much rich setting really can be valuable as a reference point for players having a hard time with the setting. Also Risen please? ^^<br /> <br /> I really want, similar to Changing Breeds 20th, a Factions of the Underworld book. I want to see it contain information on the Hierarchy, Renegades, Fanatics, Guilds, etc. I would also want to see this book address our cross over potential. Giovanni Necromancers, Encountering Werewolves in the Umbra, Orpheus, etc but also some of the weirder metaplot things, like the city of Enoch. This could possibly be a large tome being a composite of Guildbooks as well or pull the guild component out and make a single tome of Guildbooks.<br /> <br /> I kind of don't expect us Dead Heads getting many books (this is just the left over perspective from losing our game first). But after the above, I would love to see a 'Deep into that Darkness Peering' book. This would be Shadows, Spectres, Malfeans, etc. I would see this as a large book of 'monsters' but also story ideas. Kind of how God Machine Chronicle is for NWoD. <br /> <br /> Anyway, just a few thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T14:42:36-08:00","id":40741,"title":"","content":"Consolidated Arcanoi - the Great 13, the 3 Forbidden, and the exotic ones - are at the top of my list, along with an explanation of how the underworld is laid out. I want to see a clear illustration show the Shadowlands and Tempest crossover; it makes sense to me, but confounds a lot of players new to Wraith.<br /> <br /> A greater focus on games that don't involve Hierarchy membership is also high up. The best games of Wraith are those in which the freshly dead struggle in the Shadowlands, trying to resolve their Passions and Fetters. I love Stygian politics and Doomslaying as much as anyone, but they're gravy on top of the powerful core experience of the game.<br /> <br /> Risen being in the book would make me very happy indeed. On a slightly slimmer chance, I'd like to see Orphan-Grinders make their way into Wraith proper.<br /> <br /> The fantastic art that Wraith once had. V20 and W20 both had art of mixed quality, and Wraith's art was standout in capturing the mood of the underworld. I don't want to lose that. (Special mention goes to Guy Davis' work.)<br /> <br /> At least a sidebar on games after the Sixth Great Maelstrom, along with explanations other than those we are used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T11:05:16-08:00","id":41206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/34206-wraith-20th-late-2014?p=40741#post40741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fantastic art that Wraith once had. V20 and W20 both had art of mixed quality, and Wraith's art was standout in capturing the mood of the underworld. I don't want to lose that. (Special mention goes to Guy Davis' work.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh this! Yes! There are so many pieces of art which were the black and white washed out sort of pieces that always haunted my mind. Would love to get my hands on more of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}